nodecode-llmapi is a rewrite of llmapi-ai's llmapi-ai/hermes-provider-llmapi:
https://github.com/llmapi-ai/hermes-provider-llmapi
commit cc5ff07af24c1f2218a62ea5bbc1e69d3a61b8e7
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 LLM API Inc. (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider profile itself (its default base of
https://api.llmapi.ai/v1, its LLMAPI_API_KEY variable, its featured models) as
a Nodecode catalog row, one credential hook, one lane hook and one
request-header hook; the per-model wire rule (claude-* on the Anthropic
Messages API, GPT-5 and later on the Responses API, everything else on Chat
Completions) as RESOLVE-MODEL-LANE advice, so one key serves all three wires
at the one address; the public catalog read (GET /v1/models, no key, which
supplies the picker, context windows, image input, reasoning rungs and list
prices) as an hourly read cached in memory, with the original's 64K picker
floor kept and its featured models standing in while the read has not
answered; and GET /v1/credits as the /llmapi usage command, which prints the
balance, the billing mode and the monthly cap.

Left out, and why: Hermes' private seams (providers.base, ProviderProfile,
register_provider, the fetch_models / api_mode_for_model / get_model_context_length
profile methods) have no place here, so each is a Nodecode seam instead -- a
catalog row, a lane hook, a request hook. The original's error classifier,
which maps the gateway's error codes onto Hermes' own failover reasons, is
left out because Nodecode classifies a provider's refusal itself. Its
per-request cost reporting (the gateway's billed cost when the organization
turns cost-in-response on, else an estimate from the catalog's list prices) is
left out because Nodecode prices a round from the catalog row this cell
supplies. Its auxiliary model pin is left out because Nodecode names its own
auxiliary model. Catalog aliases (claude-haiku-4.5 -> claude-haiku-4-5) are
left out because the picker lists the catalog's ids, and one alias row would
list the same model twice; the gateway accepts either spelling, so a model
typed as an alias still runs.
